   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">If I have:<div><br></div><div>  data{</div><div>    matrix[N,K] x ;<div>    vector[K] z ;<br clear=\"all\"><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\">  }</div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_signature\">I can do:</div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_signature\">  transformed_data{</div><div class=\"gmail_signature\">    vector[N] y ;</div><div class=\"gmail_signature\">    y = x*z ;</div><div class=\"gmail_signature\">  }</div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_signature\">but what would I do if I have</div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div><br></div><div>  data{</div><div class=\"gmail_signature\">    vector[N] y ;</div><div>    matrix[N,K] x ;<div><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\">  }</div></div></div></div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div class=\"gmail_signature\">and I want to figure out z (given the relationship y=x*z)</div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_signature\">  transformed_data{</div><div class=\"gmail_signature\">    vector[K] z ;</div><div class=\"gmail_signature\">    z = ??? ;</div><div class=\"gmail_signature\">  }</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance!</div><div><br></div><div>Mike</div></div></div>\r\n</div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
