  {
   "id": "4_FCmY8BDgAJ",
   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2017-03-03T05:38:21Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] simple math q for transformed data section",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "If x is invertible, then you can solve for z in \r<br>\r<br> y = x * z\r<br>\r<br>as\r<br>\r<br> z = x \\ y;\r<br>\r<br>which is just a more stable and efficient version of\r<br>\r<br> z = inv(x) * y;\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>\r<br>&gt; On Mar 1, 2017, at 9:15 AM, Mike Lawrence &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mike....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "&gt; If I have:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;   data{\r<br>&gt;     matrix[N,K] x ;\r<br>&gt;     vector[K] z ;\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I can do:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;   transformed_data{\r<br>&gt;     vector[N] y ;\r<br>&gt;     y = x*z ;\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; but what would I do if I have\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;   data{\r<br>&gt;     vector[N] y ;\r<br>&gt;     matrix[N,K] x ;\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; and I want to figure out z (given the relationship y=x*z)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;   transformed_data{\r<br>&gt;     vector[K] z ;\r<br>&gt;     z = ??? ;\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; ?\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Thanks in advance!\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Mike\r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
